module nfkbTranslocationDetection
module geneExpressionDetection

manifest NIH3T3_NFkB_Cells
manifest LPS_Stock
manifest TNF_Stock
manifest CompleteMedia
manifest FibronectinSolution
manifest LPS_PulseStock
manifest TrypsinEDTA
manifest RNALysisBuffer
manifest cDNA_Primers
manifest GAPDH_Primer

// ============================================================
// Digital Signaling Decouples Activation Probability and
// Population Heterogeneity
// Kellogg RA, Tian C, Lipniacki T, Quake SR, Tay S.
// eLife 2015;4:e08931. DOI: 10.7554/eLife.08931
//
// Cell line: p65-knockout NIH 3T3 fibroblasts expressing
//   p65-DsRed (NF-kB reporter) and H2B-GFP (nuclear reporter).
//   Clonally derived to express p65-DsRed at lowest detectable
//   level to preserve near-endogenous expression.
//
// Two experimental arms are encoded in sequence:
//
// PROTOCOL 1 (BB1-BB6): LPS Dose-Modulation Experiment
//   Constant long-duration (LL) LPS stimulation at varying
//   concentrations (0.25 - 500 ng/ml), delivered via continuous
//   flow through microfluidic chambers. Modulates fraction of
//   responding cells AND NF-kB response timing/heterogeneity.
//   Duplicate chambers per condition on a single chip.
//   Stimulation by step increase in LPS via media exchange.
//   Live-cell imaging at 5-6 min intervals for ~250 min.
//   Outcome: digital (all-or-none) NF-kB activation; Hill
//   coefficient ~2.3; dose-dependent activation delay (35-80 min
//   median peak time); 5% (0.25 ng/ml) to ~100% (500 ng/ml)
//   responding cells. (Figures 2, 3)
//
// PROTOCOL 2 (BB7-BB12): LPS Duration-Modulation Experiment
//   Short-Strong (SS) pulsed LPS at constant 500 ng/ml, with
//   pulse duration varied from 1 to 40 s by washing with media
//   after each pulse duration. Controls fraction of responding
//   cells WITHOUT altering NF-kB response timing or cell-to-cell
//   variability. Outcome: 3.3% (1 s) to 87.5% (40 s) responding;
//   median peak time shifts < 2 min across all durations.
//   (Figures 4, 5, 7)
//
// PROTOCOL 3 (BB13-BB15, off-chip): Gene Expression Assay
//   Bulk 96-well plate LPS stimulation (1-500 ng/ml, 10,000
//   cells/well) for dose-dependent gene expression profiling
//   by Fluidigm qPCR (48.48 dynamic arrays). 8 target genes:
//   nfkbia, a20, nfkbie, tnf, ccl20, icam1, casp4, ccl5.
//   Normalized to GAPDH. (Figure 2E)
//
// TEMPERATURE: All cell culture and stimulation steps run at
//   37 C / 5% CO2 unless otherwise noted.
//   `heat` statements model incubator conditions.
//
// DURATION TOKENS: BioScript accepts s and m only.
//   1 day = 1440 min; used for cell seeding/growth steps.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1   main              -- device coating, cell seeding (Protocol 1)
//   BB2   llDoseHigh        -- LL high-dose LPS arm (500 ng/ml)
//   BB3   llDoseLow         -- LL low-dose LPS arm (0.25 ng/ml)
//   BB4   llDoseJoin        -- join: NF-kB detection (LL arm)
//   BB5   llPassGate        -- llSignal > 0: digital activation detected; dispose
//   BB6   llFailGate        -- llSignal <= 0: no activation; drain
//   BB7   llFinalJoin       -- join: Protocol 2 begins
//   BB8   ssPulseShort      -- SS short-pulse arm (1 s @ 500 ng/ml)
//   BB9   ssPulseLong       -- SS long-pulse arm (40 s @ 500 ng/ml)
//   BB10  ssPulseJoin       -- join: NF-kB detection (SS arm)
//   BB11  ssPassGate        -- ssSignal > 0: digital activation detected; dispose
//   BB12  ssFailGate        -- ssSignal <= 0: no activation; drain
//   BB13  ssFinalJoin       -- join: Protocol 3 (gene expression) begins
//   BB14  gexPassGate       -- gexSignal > 0: expression detected; dispose
//   BB15  gexFailGate       -- gexSignal <= 0: no expression; drain
//   BB16  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose all QC signals, experiment ends
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// Device priming, fibronectin coating, and cell seeding.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Coat microfluidic chambers with fibronectin.
//   Fibronectin solution flowed through chambers to promote
//   cell adhesion to PDMS walls. Each experimental condition
//   is measured in duplicate chambers on the chip.
//   Models channel coating by mixing priming volume of
//   fibronectin into the microfluidic chamber.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

fibronectin     = dispense 1 units of FibronectinSolution
media_prime     = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
coatedChamber   = mix fibronectin with media_prime for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Seed cells into coated chambers.
//   Approx 200 cells/chamber. Cells grown for 1 day (1440 min)
//   with periodic media replenishment until ~80% confluence.
//   `mix` abstracts channel-based cell loading; `heat` models
//   incubator growth at 37 C.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

seedCells       = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_NFkB_Cells
loadedChamber   = mix seedCells with coatedChamber for 2s

// 24 h growth to ~80% confluence at 37 C (= 1440 min).
heat loadedChamber at 37c for 1440m

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 1: LPS Dose-Modulation (LL Signal)
// Constant, long-duration stimulation at two representative
// doses: 500 ng/ml (high, ~100% cells respond) and 0.25 ng/ml
// (low, ~5% cells respond). Both are parallel branches in the
// CFG that converge at BB4 (llDoseJoin) for NF-kB detection.
//
// NOTE ON ABSTRACTION: The microfluidic chip runs all
// concentrations (0.25 - 500 ng/ml) in parallel duplicate
// chambers. BB2 and BB3 encode two representative concentrations
// as the CFG fork. The full dose-response screen is captured
// in post-processing of the nfkbTranslocationDetection readout.
//
// Stimulation: media equilibrated to 5% CO2 containing LPS
// is delivered as a step increase; ligand loss due to
// cellular internalization is replenished by continuous flow.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Dispense LPS stock solutions for dose-modulation arm.
//   LPS stock concentrations are pre-diluted off-chip in
//   CompleteMedia before loading into chip reservoirs.
//   500 ng/ml: 1.2e7 LPS molecules per cell (see Appendix Table 4).
//   0.25 ng/ml: 6.0e3 LPS molecules per cell.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsHighDose     = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock
lpsLowDose      = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock

// ============================================================
// BB2: llDoseHigh
// High-dose LL arm: 500 ng/ml continuous LPS stimulation.
// Response: ~100% cells activate; rapid onset (~35 min peak);
// low cell-to-cell timing variability; sustained oscillations
// under continuous ligand replenishment.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4a (High-dose LL): Load 500 ng/ml LPS into the chamber.
//   LPS is delivered to the sealed chamber by continuous media
//   exchange. Duration ~250 min (entire imaging window).
//   `mix` abstracts the flow-through delivery event.
//   `heat` maintains 37 C / 5% CO2 during stimulation.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

llHighChamber   = mix loadedChamber with lpsHighDose for 5s
heat llHighChamber at 37c for 250m

llHighSignal    = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on llHighChamber for 250m

// ============================================================
// BB3: llDoseLow
// Low-dose LL arm: 0.25 ng/ml continuous LPS stimulation.
// Response: ~5% cells activate; delayed onset (>80 min peak);
// high cell-to-cell timing variability (heterogeneous dynamics).
// Same stimulus area achievable via longer duration (Area Rule).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4b (Low-dose LL): Load 0.25 ng/ml LPS into the chamber.
//   Identical delivery method to high-dose arm; dose pre-diluted
//   in media before chip loading.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

llLowChamber    = mix loadedChamber with lpsLowDose for 5s
heat llLowChamber at 37c for 250m

llLowSignal     = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on llLowChamber for 250m

// ============================================================
// BB4: llDoseJoin
// Both dose arms converge here. NF-kB translocation signals
// from high- and low-dose chambers are evaluated.
// Gate is keyed on llHighSignal (highest expected signal).
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: LL Dose QC gate
// Pass (BB5): llHighSignal > 0 -> digital NF-kB activation
//             detected in at least one chamber; dispose both
//             stimulated chamber readouts.
// Fail (BB6): llHighSignal <= 0 -> no translocation signal
//             (imaging failure or no activation); drain both.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (llFinalJoin).
// ============================================================

if (llHighSignal > 0) {
    dispose llHighChamber
    dispose llLowChamber
} else {
    drain llHighChamber
    drain llLowChamber
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: llFinalJoin
// Dispose LL dose QC signals. Control falls into
// Protocol 2 (LPS Duration-Modulation / SS arm).
// ============================================================

dispose llHighSignal
dispose llLowSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 2: LPS Duration-Modulation (SS Signal)
// Pulsed LPS at constant 500 ng/ml; pulse duration varied
// from 1 to 40 s. Chambers washed with media after each pulse.
// Controls fraction of responding cells WITHOUT affecting
// NF-kB response timing or cell-to-cell variability.
//
// Two representative pulse durations encoded as CFG branches:
//   BB8:  1 s pulse  -> ~3.3% cells activate (few active)
//   BB9: 40 s pulse  -> ~87.5% cells activate (many active)
// Branches converge at BB10 (ssPulseJoin) for NF-kB detection.
//
// Key result: despite >25x difference in responding fraction,
// median peak time changes by < 2 min between 1 s and 40 s.
// This contrasts with LL dose modulation where peak time
// shifts > 35 min from 0.25 to 500 ng/ml.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Prepare fresh cells in new chambers for SS arm.
//   Same seeding protocol as Protocol 1. Fresh LPS pulse
//   stock (500 ng/ml) is pre-loaded. Media wash solution
//   is in a parallel reservoir for post-pulse washing.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

ssCells         = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_NFkB_Cells
ssMedia         = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
ssChamber       = mix ssCells with ssMedia for 2s
heat ssChamber at 37c for 1440m

// SS pulse stock: 500 ng/ml LPS for both short and long pulse arms.
ssPulseHigh     = dispense 1 units of LPS_PulseStock
ssPulseLong40   = dispense 1 units of LPS_PulseStock

// Media wash: flowed through chamber immediately after pulse
// to remove LPS (no further receptor occupancy after pulse end).
// Abstracts the post-pulse wash by mixing in fresh media.
mediaWashShort  = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
mediaWashLong   = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia

// ============================================================
// BB8: ssPulseShort
// 1 s pulse at 500 ng/ml LPS.
// LPS delivered for exactly 1 s then washed out with media.
// Result: ~3.3% cells activate; rapid, synchronous responses
// in the small activating fraction. Same responding fraction
// as 0.25 ng/ml continuous LL stimulation (Fig 5B vs Fig 2D).
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6a (1 s SS pulse): Deliver 1 s LPS pulse, then wash.
//   `mix for 1s` abstracts the 1 s flow of LPS through the
//   chamber at 500 ng/ml. Media wash immediately follows
//   to terminate receptor-ligand contact.
//   Post-wash: chamber sealed; imaging at 5-6 min intervals.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 1 s LPS pulse (500 ng/ml): flow-through event.
ss1sPulsed      = mix ssChamber with ssPulseHigh for 1s
// Immediate media wash to terminate stimulus.
ss1sWashed      = mix ss1sPulsed with mediaWashShort for 5s

// Image for 150 min post-pulse (NF-kB peak occurs ~50 min).
heat ss1sWashed at 37c for 150m
ss1sSignal      = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on ss1sWashed for 150m

// ============================================================
// BB9: ssPulseLong
// 40 s pulse at 500 ng/ml LPS.
// LPS delivered for 40 s then washed out with media.
// Result: ~87.5% cells activate; rapid, uniform responses
// (low timing variability). Median peak time ~47 min.
// Identical single-cell dynamics shape to 1 s pulse arm;
// only the responding fraction differs.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6b (40 s SS pulse): Deliver 40 s LPS pulse, then wash.
//   Same method as 1 s arm; only pulse duration changes.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// 40 s LPS pulse (500 ng/ml): flow-through event.
ss40sPulsed     = mix ssChamber with ssPulseLong40 for 40s
// Immediate media wash to terminate stimulus.
ss40sWashed     = mix ss40sPulsed with mediaWashLong for 5s

// Image for 150 min post-pulse (NF-kB peak occurs ~47 min).
heat ss40sWashed at 37c for 150m
ss40sSignal     = detect nfkbTranslocationDetection on ss40sWashed for 150m

// ============================================================
// BB10: ssPulseJoin
// Both SS pulse arms converge here. Gate keyed on ss40sSignal
// (highest expected responding fraction and amplitude).
// ============================================================

// ============================================================
// BB11 / BB12: SS Pulse QC gate
// Pass (BB11): ss40sSignal > 0 -> digital NF-kB activation
//              detected in >=1 chamber; dispose both readouts.
// Fail (BB12): ss40sSignal <= 0 -> no translocation signal
//              (imaging or reagent failure); drain both.
// Both branches converge at BB13 (ssFinalJoin).
// ============================================================

if (ss40sSignal > 0) {
    dispose ss1sWashed
    dispose ss40sWashed
} else {
    drain ss1sWashed
    drain ss40sWashed
}

// ============================================================
// BB13: ssFinalJoin
// Dispose SS pulse QC signals. Control falls into
// Protocol 3 (off-chip gene expression assay).
// ============================================================

dispose ss1sSignal
dispose ss40sSignal

// ============================================================
// PROTOCOL 3: Gene Expression Assay (off-chip, 96-well plate)
// Dose-dependent NF-kB gene expression profiling under LPS
// stimulation. Two representative doses: 500 ng/ml and 50 ng/ml.
//
// Off-chip workflow:
//   - 10,000 cells/well seeded in 96-well plate overnight.
//   - Stimulated with LPS at the indicated concentration.
//   - Lysed at time points from 0 to 8 h post-stimulation.
//   - RNA reverse-transcribed with Invitrogen One-Step RT-PCR kit.
//   - cDNA pre-amplified (specific target amplification,
//     24-primer set).
//   - Quantitative PCR on 48.48 Fluidigm dynamic arrays
//     (technical duplicates per sample).
//   - Expression normalized to GAPDH.
//
// Target genes and their response class:
//   Early  (peak 0.5-1 h):  nfkbia, a20
//   Early  (peak 1-2 h):    nfkbie, tnf
//   Intermediate (1-3 h):   ccl20, icam1
//   Late   (slow kinetics): casp4, ccl5
//
// NOTE: Late genes (casp4, ccl5) do not reflect the delayed
// NF-kB activation because their induction kinetics are slow.
// Early and intermediate genes show dose-dependent delay
// consistent with NF-kB translocation data (Figure 2E).
//
// NOTE ON ABSTRACTION: 96-well plate seeding and LPS delivery
// are abstracted using `dispense` and `mix`; `heat` models the
// incubator. Cell lysis, RNA extraction, and qPCR steps are
// modelled as sequential mix + detect operations.
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Seed cells into 96-well plate and attach overnight.
//   10,000 cells/well; 37 C overnight = 1440 min (1 day).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bulkCells       = dispense 1 units of NIH3T3_NFkB_Cells
bulkMedia       = dispense 1 units of CompleteMedia
bulkWell        = mix bulkCells with bulkMedia for 1m
heat bulkWell at 37c for 1440m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: Stimulate with LPS (500 ng/ml; high-dose arm).
//   LPS added directly to wells; incubated at 37 C.
//   Cells lysed at 0, 0.5, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8 h time points.
//   Here encoded as a single 8 h (480 min) stimulation
//   window; time-resolved lysis is abstracted by detection
//   module (geneExpressionDetection).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsGex500       = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock
stimWell500     = mix bulkWell with lpsGex500 for 5s
heat stimWell500 at 37c for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: Stimulate with LPS (50 ng/ml; low-dose arm).
//   Parallel well. Identical protocol; different LPS dose.
//   Low dose induces dose-dependent delay in early gene peaks
//   (e.g., nfkbia peak shifts from 30 min to 1 h; IkBe from
//   1 h to 2 h; ccl20 from 1 h to 2-3 h).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lpsGex50        = dispense 1 units of LPS_Stock
stimWell50      = mix bulkWell with lpsGex50 for 5s
heat stimWell50 at 37c for 480m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 10: Lyse cells and prepare RNA for qPCR.
//   RNALysisBuffer added to each well; RNA reverse-transcribed
//   and cDNA pre-amplified. Modelled as mix steps.
//   geneExpressionDetection abstracts Fluidigm qPCR readout
//   (48.48 dynamic array; normalization to GAPDH).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysate500       = dispense 1 units of RNALysisBuffer
lysate50        = dispense 1 units of RNALysisBuffer
primers500      = dispense 1 units of cDNA_Primers
primers50       = dispense 1 units of cDNA_Primers
gapdh500        = dispense 1 units of GAPDH_Primer
gapdh50         = dispense 1 units of GAPDH_Primer

// Lysis and cDNA prep.
rna500          = mix stimWell500 with lysate500 for 5m
cdna500         = mix rna500 with primers500 for 30m
cdnaNorm500     = mix cdna500 with gapdh500 for 5s

rna50           = mix stimWell50 with lysate50 for 5m
cdna50          = mix rna50 with primers50 for 30m
cdnaNorm50      = mix cdna50 with gapdh50 for 5s

// Fluidigm qPCR: detect gene expression signal.
// geneExpressionDetection module abstracts 48.48 dynamic array
// qPCR with technical duplicates. Signal > 0 indicates
// detectable expression above GAPDH-normalized baseline.
gexSignal500    = detect geneExpressionDetection on cdnaNorm500 for 60m
gexSignal50     = detect geneExpressionDetection on cdnaNorm50 for 60m

// ============================================================
// BB14 / BB15: Gene expression QC gate
// Pass (BB14): gexSignal500 > 0 -> detectable NF-kB-dependent
//              gene expression at high dose; dispose readouts.
// Fail (BB15): gexSignal500 <= 0 -> no expression detected
//              (RT-PCR or Fluidigm failure); drain all.
// Both branches converge at BB16 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (gexSignal500 > 0) {
    dispose cdnaNorm500
    dispose cdnaNorm50
} else {
    drain cdnaNorm500
    drain cdnaNorm50
}

// ============================================================
// BB16: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose all gene expression QC signals.
// Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose gexSignal500
dispose gexSignal50

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
